From eb78ee1668b0b3a97beabe21902c0b285d4c9d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:32:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 13/40] Gate resident face capture and operator onboarding face
 with liveness

Before the SBI face capture, only for the Face tile:
- biometric_capture_scan_block_portrait.dart (Scan): RESIDENT.
- biometric_scan_middle_block.dart, the landscape (tablet) layout of the
  same resident capture (Scan, and Rescan in the scan dialog): RESIDENT.
  Leaving it ungated would let a rotated device skip liveness.
- operator_biometric_capture_scan_block_view.dart (Scan): OPERATOR.
Not proceeding (cancelled or blocked) returns before any capture, so no
SBI call and no capture attempt is counted; the liveness screen already
showed the recovery text when blocked.

The exception photo is not gated: it belongs to the biometric exception
process, the recovery path the resident recovery text points to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
